<td colspan="3" class="mytext">So you're interested in Joining the BloodHorde....
<p>The Horde is an Evil Only Roleplay oriented guild on Terris Thule. It is amoung the Oldest guilds on the server, orginiating on the Karana server before the server split that created Terris. It is a family oriented guild with close ties between members - so if you're looking for a Ph4t Lewt Uber Guild please don't bother contacting us. Still, our strong core membership and allied raid partners still allow the BloodHorde to raid parts of the &quot;high end game&quot; while retaining the community bonds garnered by a roleplay guild.</p>

<p>Applicant Guidelines:<br>						
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any class from the Dark Elf, Troll, Ogre, or Iksar races <br>						2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Shadow Knights and Necros from any race <br>						3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Clerics of Cazic Thule or Bertoxxulus religions <br>						4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Characters must be at least level 24  <br>						
<br>
If your character does not fall within those guidelines, chances are that we will not accept you. Bloodhorde is a role-play evil-only guild. Many of our members are in Bloodhorde for the main purpose that they can role-play evil. If we were to allow non-evil characters within the guild, we would severely disrupt the overall role-play environment for our members. If you really want to be in Bloodhorde, you need a character that fits those guidelines.Note that Bloodhorde will not offer any &quot;power leveling&quot; services. An individual member may offer to help, but the guild overall will not promise anything of that nature.<br>
<br>						
The basic recruiting procedure for new members is as follows:<br>						
<br>						
1. The potential recruit must hunt with a member of the Horde. During this time the Horde member will review the recruits compatibility (socially and from a Roleplaying standpoint).<br>			<br>
2. After the member(s) the recruit has partnered with have consented, the recruit is brought into the guild at the rank of 'minion'.  The 'minion' rank lasts for a length of 21 days, after which the officership convenes to decide whether the member belongs in the Horde.  At this point the minion must have the approval of at least 2 Horde members, who will vouch on his or her behalf.  Additionally, any members who have feel they have reason to disallow the minion's membership (based on the rules of the Guild, outlined on the website) are able to present their issues now for review.<br>						<br>						3. Once approved, the Minion must endure his or her Trial of Blood. Trials of blood occur once a month at the monthly guild meeting (which will be announced with at least 5 days notice). If you cannot attend the monthly meeting please let one of the Officers know so that alternate arrangements can be made (we understand that everyone has obligations outside of the Horde, and as long as notice is given accommodations will be made).</p>					<p>We accept players from all over the world, but the majority of Horde members are located in North America, so raids tend to be scheduled around that. Standard raid times are Sunday at Noon EST and Wednesday at 9pm EST.  Members are in no way obliged to attend raids - they are welcome to come to as many or as few as they wish, bearing in  in mind that priority for raid level support and gear is given to those who raid more frequently over casual or non raiders.</p>					
<p>
</p>

